    "result_text": "The build is green. The test suite passes (1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the per-city owner-capacity rule following the repo's existing owner-validation pattern (which already had `DuplicateTelephoneException` / `DuplicateHouseholdException` producing 409s).\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`CityOwnerLimitException.java`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` carrying the offending city, mirroring the existing duplicate exceptions.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, added a `requireCityHasCapacity(owner.getCity())` check (run right after mapping, before save). The new helper counts existing owners whose city matches case-insensitively (reusing the existing `equalsIgnoreCase` helper, consistent with `generateCustomerCode`) and throws `CityOwnerLimitException` when the count is `>= 50`. Added a `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY = 50` constant.\n\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 added `@ExceptionHandler(CityOwnerLimitException.class)` returning **409 Conflict** with `errors: [\"city\"]`, matching how the other owner conflicts are reported.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreRejectsWhenCityAtCapacity` (fills a fresh city to exactly 50, then expects the 51st create to return 409) passes, and the full suite is green.",
