        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots into the existing conventions of this controller cleanly and additively:\n\n- `requireCityHasCapacity` is a direct structural sibling of the existing `requireUniqueTelephone`, `requireUniqueHousehold`, and `countNamesakes` helpers \u2014 same shape (a private `requireX`/count guard over `clinicService.findAllOwners().stream()`), same case-insensitive comparison via the already-present `equalsIgnoreCase` helper, and it's invoked from `addOwner` alongside the other create-time guards. A maintainer would expect exactly this. No new logic is duplicated \u2014 it reuses `equalsIgnoreCase` rather than reinventing it.\n- The `MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY` constant is placed and documented consistently with the neighboring `EMAIL_PATTERN` / `ADDRESS_ABBREVIATIONS` constants.\n- `CityOwnerLimitException` mirrors the existing `DuplicateTelephoneException` / `DuplicateHouseholdException` pattern (same package, carries the offending value, extends `RuntimeException`), and its handler in `ExceptionControllerAdvice` is a faithful copy of the existing 409 handlers (same logging shape, `detailBuild`, `setProperty(\"errors\", ...)`, `CONFLICT`).\n\nBusiness logic living in the controller rather than the service layer is a pre-existing convention here (every create-time rule is a private controller helper), so following it is the coherent choice; relocating it would be re-architecting the surrounding code, not reviewing this addition. The structure is already clean."
